Build secondary indices only when consumed

Keep primary tuple storage eager and retain secondary indices with their
source snapshots. Catch up on demand using borrowed, sharing-aware tree
differences instead of materializing temporary difference trees.

Publish primary snapshots for strata and share derived indices between
consumers of the same snapshot. Defer secondary reads through rule
environments so empty joins can avoid constructing unused indices.
Propagate native model facts through primary indices and derive other
orders and diagonals lazily. Keep simultaneous scheduling the default.

Cover sparse tree edits, mapped comparisons, snapshot identity, delayed
reads, equality replacements, and dynamic import. Leave canonicalization
branch updates for separate work.
